{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3230","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3230","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3230\",\"parent_revision\":\"135ce36942a578206684ad80a1d07aa7d7cae628\",\"root_revision\":\"6b8a706f0da7fc5f887ea6e173b250a69517dd1f13d95eec88df3b5fad31a5a2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-24\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`close_item()` (`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py`, function starting ~line 3107) accepts `reference: str = \\\"\\\"` and `comment: str = \\\"\\\"` parameters, documented as optional dismissal context (e.g. the duplicate or superseding item a `duplicate`/`superseded` close reason refers to). Neither reaches the caller's actual intent on any backend, verified by direct read.\\n\\n**The `reference` parameter is shadowed before use.** Line ~3153: `reference = item.reference` reassigns the local name to the item's own backend storage reference (a file path or backend id) \u2014 overwriting the caller-supplied `reference` argument entirely. The overwritten value is what gets forwarded to `close_github_issue(issue_ref, reason, reference=reference, comment=comment, ...)` a few lines later, so the GitHub close comment's \\\"Reference:\\\" line always shows the item's own reference to itself, never the related item the caller named.\\n\\n**Neither parameter is persisted to local metadata on any backend.** `update_item_metadata(reference, {\\\"metadata\\\": {\\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\", \\\"close_reason\\\": reason}}, output=out)` writes only `status` and `close_reason` \u2014 no `reference` or `comment` key. So even where the shadowing bug didn't exist, these two parameters would still be invisible to SQLite, Memory, and Beads backends, which never call `close_github_issue` at all (that call is gated on `if issue_ref:`).\\n\\n**Net effect per backend:**\\n- GitHub: `comment` is rendered correctly into the close comment (`gh_client.py`'s `close_github_issue`, ~line 1295-1317, appends it verbatim when non-empty). `reference` renders, but always as the item's own self-reference, never the caller's intended cross-reference.\\n- SQLite, Memory, Beads: both parameters are silently discarded. No trace of them anywhere.\\n\\n**Where this was found**: a review of `plugins/development-harness/CONTEXT.md`'s Close glossary entry (PR #3221) initially stated Close records \\\"optional `reference` and `comment` for dismissal context\\\" as if this worked as documented. Codex correctly flagged that the fields exist as parameters but the contract isn't honored. The glossary entry has been corrected to describe the actual (broken) behavior with a pointer to this issue rather than the intended one.\\n\\nPoints needing design decisions during grooming, not pre-decided here: whether `reference` should mean \\\"the related item, distinct from the item's own storage reference\\\" (requiring the shadowing line to be removed or renamed) or whether the parameter's purpose should be redefined to match what it currently and accidentally does; and whether `comment`/`reference` belong in the neutral `BacklogItemMetadata` schema (following the pattern #3220 already establishes for Resolve's evidence trail) so dismissal context survives on every backend, not only GitHub.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Codex review on PR #3221, verified against source 2026-08-24\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"53c396de76bfad66f7f4a0ec70b3282d3ec41358f0e8635e7672e2541046a089\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRP6rAQ\"}"}